{
  "file": "crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Fingerprinting]/fn[fingerprint]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "These storage and output-decoding checks use records with no content\n dependencies. The required fingerprint callback must remain unused:\n consulting graph contents would mask a storage-layer or decoding error.\n Other domain fixtures exercise tracked fingerprint observations."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/storage.rs` `impl[StoredGraph/Fingerprinting]/fn[fingerprint]` is a valid coverage exception.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced `:::{cite}` block with commentary on an explicit function with a body, which is what the built-in allows. The function is a guard that only calls `panic!`, so zero execution is its intended state.\n- **Substantive reason:** `Fingerprinting` requires the callback (`trait[Fingerprinting]` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph.rs`). The real callers, `InspectionContext::prepare_read` and `record_is_current`, call `fingerprint` after `node_content`. The `StoredGraph` fixture is meant for storage delegation and output decoding only. Reaching the guard would mean the storage test had wandered into graph content, so leaving it unused is the point. This is more than difficulty.\n- **Agreement with the source:**\n  - `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_current_bad_outputs_are_output_errors` runs the validator on records produced by `StoredReview::execute`. That function records no dependencies, so `record_is_current` never reaches the fingerprint callback.\n  - `consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path` only calls `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`. Neither resolves content.\n  - The shared `record()` fixture includes a `Dependency::Node`. The commentary's \"no content dependencies\" is therefore loose for that fixture. It is only stored and loaded, never checked for currentness, so the callback is never reached and the claim holds in substance.\n- **Other fixtures:** `tests/contracts.rs` `fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` exercises real fingerprint observations, as the commentary says.\n\nI found no gap.",
